      "content": "When you're looking at a house, escrow acts as a neutral third party holding the funds from both you and the seller until all the conditions of the sale are met and the house closes. The escrow agent is responsible for making sure that each party fulfills their part of the deal, such as transferring the deed and ensuring any repairs or contingencies are taken care of. This helps to protect both you and the seller, ensuring that the terms of the agreement are respected before finalizing the purchase.",
